 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Singularity:** The covariance matrix $\Sigma_i$ must be invertible for the alpha calculation. If singular, a fallback or regularization is required [G].
-*   **Single-view Overfitting:** Relying on a single view can lead to excessive densification due to occlusions or transient artifacts. The multi-view aggregation mitigates this [S1].
-*   **Gradient vs. Alpha:** Conventional gradient metrics may modify Gaussians with low visibility. Alpha-weighting ensures only visible, contributing Gaussians are modified [S1].
